 :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562084} {:answer/id #uuid "d52aa83e-9bf0-5b70-838b-ebb02d4dc2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562115}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561766} :answer-field/id #uuid "762648f5-1207-5f3e-be39-97bd8eb92965" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562299} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24ef6fa3-0c61-52da-9a58-b5f3581e26c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561681} {:answer/id #uuid "8c693a99-512e-5061-a753-dd7c3e3b934c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561932} {:answer/id #uuid "8fbe3370-6854-5660-a4dd-b09e0e41ba13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561940} {:answer/id #uuid "d65518ad-4812-5740-95e3-1539e00df576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562116} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c42440-43d6-5af8-9771-f53fa953e398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562162}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561940} :answer-field/id #uuid "95323910-156c-5adf-a3a0-32d0fac9f9e0" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e335f33f-c98e-5cab-bfc9-af13ddc0ea7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-334872" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=2x(1-x)-xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-2y+4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[0.5,\\,1]^{T},$ we get\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$J({x}^{∗})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,.$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are \n{{field-5}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}$ is \n{{field-6}}{{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote ${f}_{1}(x,y)=2x(1-x)-xy$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=-2y+4xy.$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x(1-x)-xy)=2-4x-y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x(1-x)-xy)=-x \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2y+4xy)=4y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y+4xy)=-2+4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the Jacobian matrix is\n\n$$\nJ=[\\begin{aligned}2-4x-y & -x \\\\ 4y & -2+4x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}0.5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\nJ({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}2-4(0.5)-(1) & -(0.5) \\\\ 4(1) & -2+4(0.5)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -0.5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix, we write down the characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -0.5 \\\\ 4 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-4\\cdot (-0.5) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation, we get the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1,2}=-0.5\\pm 0.5\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}.$ Since the eigenvalues are complex with negative real parts, our equilibrium is $\\text{an asymptotically stable}$ $\\text{spiral sink}.$"} :step/id #uuid "7f546ceb-808c-5bc5-becd-cf02fd535255" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562555}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562555 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167254 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "920b1022-bc85-5441-9714-70e679a31b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164672} {:answer/id #uuid "af366199-e291-55b1-a9e6-f8155d482a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164673} {:answer/id #uuid "2ef29150-0133-59f4-87d9-4c2cba3fae74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164674} {:answer/id #uuid "73208ed5-4d23-51ea-bc9a-19eb824f5cfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164675} {:answer/id #uuid "7c285afd-2a31-5435-bbd4-df521c8153ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164676}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186164676} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9222123-e818-5157-8b30-966d55e74bf0" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a34a68d1-e3ec-5378-85e0-fafc41a989b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164678} {:answer/id #uuid "d92961e1-e234-5ecf-952d-a5604d5e4b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164679} {:answer/id #uuid "0077aa4a-b5d3-5e45-9581-99842a25eace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164680} {:answer/id #uuid "1eb6ce64-806a-5881-aa0d-c8ece780385a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164681} {:answer/id #uuid "3b29d53a-f2c9-5abf-ab08-52db925ad8aa" :answer/type