id #edb/ref 17592186164691} :answer-field/id #uuid "814848ec-9fc3-5950-a8d4-b6c060000459" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e4da0a6-c552-5d38-9593-70e060d2e5bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561812} {:answer/id #uuid "a048225d-f025-5876-910a-c4ed7422a0b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561978} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a947d2-68eb-5c1a-9545-3d0e64145497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1,2}=-1\\pm \\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561998} {:answer/id #uuid "d926e717-6de1-5aa1-9abb-8be9de358890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1,2}=\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562124}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561812} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d187d12-3bb7-50db-8d48-0c10bc1370ff" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562279} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a77f178-0d9d-5486-b59c-97b003151b7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "an asymptotically stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561928} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d60a15-2a3c-510a-baca-661590169505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "a stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562109} {:answer/id #uuid "eae2b68c-bf5a-5a2b-94e7-2bef06db3eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "an unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562170}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562170} :answer-field/id #uuid "72c97790-bd95-5f2a-ad72-b18a6cd6672f" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562294} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10dd0b08-b68d-54c8-8087-e11b5607aeda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "saddle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561635} {:answer/id #uuid "403c9eba-0a6c-5235-881d-c1cc9fb065ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561739} {:answer/id #uuid "49ba274e-d797-55ad-bdb1-d3b638c103d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "source" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561771} {:answer/id #uuid "69ef2487-a4a8-5651-92af-99ff9edca9e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "sink" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561848}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561635} :answer-field/id #uuid "73aec003-f39a-520d-adb3-80d245644c7f" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f98673ec-d1ca-550a-94d6-d4c7a722e79f" :question/math-academy-id "q-334877" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=2x(1-4x)-xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-2y+4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[0,\\,0]^{T},$ we get\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$J({x}^{∗})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,.$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are \n{{field-5}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}$ is \n{{field-6}}{{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote ${f}_{1}(x,y)=2x(1-4x)-xy$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=-2y+4xy.$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x(1-4x)-xy)=2-16x-y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x(1-4x)-xy)=-x \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2y+4xy)=4y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y+4xy)=-2+4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the Jacobian matrix is\n\n$$\nJ=[\\begin{aligned}2-16x-y & -x \\\\ 4y & -2+4x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\nJ({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}2-16(0)-(0) & -(0) \\\\ 4(0) & -2+4(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{ and }{\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$ Since the eigenvalues are real with opposite signs, our equilibrium is $\\text{an unstable}$ $\\text{saddle}.$"} :step/id #uuid "81c1df34-ad18-5252-bc8d-00804c2ca251" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562564}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562564 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12605135-005f-5c7e-a333-ccd92d038487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561638}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561638} :answer-field/id #uuid "c31e99f2-faff-5c92-ade4-f80823484907" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562348} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b312fd2e-6af0-53c1-bfcb-3a2a4c0a9b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562030}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562030} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf12e9a4-1722-522c-b0b9-24a73d73f98d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0c74a5e-fdb7-5051-9117-0bccadb4292e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562182}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562182} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef3a4ab3-90c5-58e4-98ed-cbdc12d7b736" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3721367d-c322-5ae9-9c82-a2cb18aa384c" :question/math-academy-id "q-335594" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=2x(1-0.1x)-xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-3y+xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. The equilibria of the model are the following:\n\n$(0,0),\\,(${{field-1}}$,0),\\,(${{field-2}}$,${{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x(1-0.1x)-xy=0 \\\\ -3y+xy=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y+xy & =0 \\\\ y(-3+x) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y=0$ or $x=3.$ We consider both cases separately.\n\n- If $y=0,$ substituting it into the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x(1-0.1x)-x(0) & =0 \\\\ 2x(0.1x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the first two equilibria are $(0,0)$ and $(10,0).$\n\n- If $x=3,$ substituting it into the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)(1-0.1(3))-(3)y & =0 \\\\ 4.2-3y & =0 \\\\ y & =1.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, another equilibrium is $(3,1.4).$\n\nTherefore, the equilibria of the model are\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(10,0),\\,(3,1.4).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ad127185-be66-5e16-bb79-eea3f103e5a6"}] :activity/title "The Lotka-Volterra Model With Carrying Capacity" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561569}]}
